{"id": "EUVD-2026-86785", "enisaUuid": "c7428915-7f08-33cd-8bd5-4141a9aa4a37", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: us122l: Prevent write upgrades for read mappings\n\nThe hwdep mmap callback rejects read-buffer mappings that are initially\nwritable, but leaves VM_MAYWRITE set on mappings created with PROT_READ.\nA process that can open the hwdep node O_RDWR can later use mprotect() to\nmake the mapping writable.\n\nThe read allocation begins with struct usb_stream. Its read_size member is\nused by the fault handler to decide which pages belong to the read buffer.\nThe read VMA intentionally remains expandable because pcm_usb_stream uses\nmremap() after reading that size. Changing read_size first can therefore\nmap and access pages beyond the allocation. The same member is also\nconsumed by usb_stream_free(), where changing it can make\nfree_pages_exact() release pages outside the allocation.\n\nClear VM_MAYWRITE for read-buffer mappings after rejecting an initially\nwritable VMA. This keeps the separate output-buffer mapping writable while\npreventing later permission upgrades.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:58", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbc1f954ce67d739d41d1f0757d29850353ebb6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/becb89036a1320ef0a77da2d27935ac0704345c4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a5f5a5a32c78e67701f1d0f26bc87af68895604", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/938e8d6cee8d36f24669dfdcd3717e081eb32d64", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64a87950239867682cde128020e1a47088295e5c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d9c537b14f4982f17b103e3a2cfeee4bee6bc026", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0eb9dd4774af0ac4d1fd105ef2b0a1f6cec06f2f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71c610aeb1770302ac9c9e0b9a4ecd37f1311928"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97931", "GHSA-vp4m-4hj6-cc9p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0451d723-467b-3105-baa6-f26414f4ad3a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "170704b4-9d68-3915-bd13-3c8c8cce4be2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "26000cac-d5cf-3014-82d5-549370dd73f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "030a07e441296c372f946cd4065b5d831d8dc40c <0eb9dd4774af0ac4d1fd105ef2b0a1f6cec06f2f"}, {"id": "4d88c925-2ff4-3a8f-a522-7f5cfd650e6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.28"}, {"id": "5ce397d1-bffe-3b0e-8af5-c3ad53ec791b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "030a07e441296c372f946cd4065b5d831d8dc40c <6a5f5a5a32c78e67701f1d0f26bc87af68895604"}, {"id": "6094e71a-1154-3f6d-99da-9b76e2ce2e04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6a7d4a62-e552-37e6-b20c-b9559cd744e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "7c13a6ef-db28-3cc4-9df6-3aadafeb6976", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "030a07e441296c372f946cd4065b5d831d8dc40c <71c610aeb1770302ac9c9e0b9a4ecd37f1311928"}, {"id": "820e71d0-3c86-3f7d-afa0-24592707e32c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "82d49d62-9298-31d8-82b0-a266bd3fdf8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8328d718-29d9-335c-b0e9-d28183966dea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "885851eb-5446-3e94-93de-f87a7f5a9c69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "030a07e441296c372f946cd4065b5